# Code Review

When asked to review code, analyze ALL of the following areas on every modified file. Enforce all rules defined in the referenced rule files.
Report each check using this format:

- **✅ Passed** — compliant
- **⚠️ Warning** — suggestion, non-blocking
- **🔴 Violation** — must fix before push

---

## 1. Architecture & Layer Separation

> Enforce constraints defined in `project-context.mdc` § Architectural Constraints.

- Verify dependency direction: no upward or outward imports.
- Verify `shared/` folder usage for cross-layer elements.
- Verify repository interfaces in `domain/`, implementations in `data/`.
- Verify ViewModel communicates only with domain layer.
- Verify UI layer contains zero business logic.
- Verify no cross-feature imports outside `core/`.

## 2. Dart Code Quality

> Enforce all rules in `coding-conventions.mdc` and `dart-rules.mdc`.

## 3. Null Safety

> Enforce null safety rules in `coding-conventions.mdc` § Null Safety.

## 4. Flutter Widget Quality

> Enforce all rules in `ui-rules.mdc` §§ General Principles, Page Rules, Widget Rules, Composition.

## 5. State Management (Riverpod)

- One provider per file.
- Providers scoped appropriately (feature-level vs. global).
- `AsyncValue` used for all async states (loading / error / data).
- `ref.watch` inside `build()` for reactive UI. `ref.read` only inside callbacks and event handlers.
- `autoDispose` used when the provider should not outlive its consumer.
- No direct state mutation — use Notifier methods exclusively.

## 6. Error Handling

> Enforce error handling rules in `coding-conventions.mdc` § Error Handling.

Additionally verify:
- User-facing errors produce UI feedback (dialog, snackbar, or error widget).
- Custom domain exceptions are used instead of generic `Exception`.

## 7. Performance

> Enforce performance rules in `ui-rules.mdc` § Performance.

Additionally verify:
- No unnecessary `setState()` or provider rebuilds.
- Images use caching (`CachedNetworkImage` or equivalent).
- No full widget tree rebuilds — use `const`, `select()`, or granular providers.
- Animations use `AnimatedBuilder` or `AnimatedWidget`, not parent rebuilds.

## 8. Security

- No credentials, API keys, or secrets in the codebase.
- No sensitive data in logs or print statements.
- User input validated and sanitized before processing.
- Sensitive persisted data uses encryption, not plain text.

## 9. Platform & Responsiveness

> Enforce responsive rules in `ui-rules.mdc` § Responsive Design.

## 10. Dependencies & Imports

- No unused dependencies in `pubspec.yaml`.
- Import order: `dart:` → `package:flutter/` → `package:` (third-party) → project relative imports.
- Prefer relative imports within the same feature.
- No circular dependencies between features.
- New packages must be justified (maintenance, popularity, null-safety).

